  "mechanism": "Per km, cruise time is load-independent (163.6 s/km) while energy is a0 + a1*n (n passengers onboard). An insertion's energy increment is therefore approximately a0*dD + a1*dPK + stop terms, and its duration increment dD/v + stop/dwell terms. Only a1*dPK (added passenger-km) is not proportional to duration, so the lever is rho = a1/a0. Uniformly scaling all energy costs would only re-weight alpha_E, which the energy-only probe showed cannot exceed about 2% saving. Payload changes rho, i.e. the non-proportional share.",
  "design": {
    "seeds": "601001:700001:1000",
    "fleet_configs": [
      {
        "id": "V12R100",
        "vehicles": 12,
        "requests": 100
      }
    ],
    "mass_configs": [
